        drop
table ip dormant (nft)
  chain c: filter hook input priority 0 policy drop (not running)
    tcp dport 22 accept
        match l4proto in {6}
        match dport in {22}
        accept
    reject
        reject
    reject
        reject
    icmp type echo-request accept
        match l4proto in {1}
        match icmp-type in {8}
        accept
    ip protocol tcp accept
        match l4proto in {6}
        accept
    meta l4proto udp accept
        match l4proto in {17}
        accept
table ip6 six (nft)
  chain in6: filter hook input priority -5 policy drop
    tcp dport 22 accept
        match l4proto in {6}
        match dport in {22}
        accept
    ip6 saddr 2001:db8:99::/64 udp dport 53 accept
        match saddr in {2001:db8:99::/64}
        match l4proto in {17}
        match dport in {53}
        accept
    meta l4proto ipv6-icmp accept
        match l4proto in {58}
        accept
    icmpv6 type { nd-router-advert, nd-neighbor-solicit } accept
        match l4proto in {58}
        match icmpv6-type in {134, 135}
        accept
    reject
        reject
    reject
        reject
set @inet/t/auto {192.0.2.0/24, 203.0.113.5}
set @inet/t/cmt {198.51.100.11, 198.51.100.12}
set @inet/t/dmap {80}
set @inet/t/empty {}
set @inet/t/ifwild {"eth"*, "lo"}
set @inet/t/macs INCOMPLETE the set macs holds values of a kind seaward does not model (hardware (MAC) addresses) {}
set @inet/t/markmap {198.51.100.7}
set @inet/t/marks {1, 2}
set @inet/t/net6 {2001:db8:1::1-2001:db8:1::ff, 2001:db8:99::/64}
set @inet/t/protos {6, 17, 47}
set @inet/t/states {2, 4}
set @inet/t/tmo dynamic {198.51.100.9, 198.51.100.10}
set @inet/t/ty {198.51.100.7 . 22}
set @inet/t/vcatch {22 : accept, * : drop}
set @inet/t/vconcat {198.51.100.0/24 . 22 : accept, 192.0.2.7 . 80-90 : drop}
set @inet/t/vif {"docker0" : accept, "eth0" : jump side}
note: the arp table ar was left out: it filters ARP packets, which seaward does not follow
note: the flowtable ft of table inet t was left out: it only speeds up connections that the rules already let through
note: the chain egress0 of table netdev nd was left out: it has no rules and lets everything pass
note: the chain fw of table bridge br was left out: it filters frames switched between the ports of a bridge, which never enter the packet path seaward follows
note: the table ip dormant is switched off (flags dormant): the kernel runs none of its chains, so seaward does not either
unfollowed: in lo only-stops walked: the chain ing of table inet t acts on packets as they pass lo, underneath the bridge, bond or VLAN interface they arrive on, where seaward does not follow them
unfollowed: in lo only-stops walked: the chain ingress0 of table netdev nd acts on packets as they pass lo, underneath the bridge, bond or VLAN interface they arrive on, where seaward does not follow them
